Market Challenges
Measurement consistency can be affected by lead quality, contact conditions and temperature variation. Instrument manufacturers must deliver repeatable readings across different battery chemistries and operating environments. Integration with production systems and the need for traceable test records can also increase technical requirements.

Market Restraints
High implementation and qualification costs can limit adoption among smaller battery manufacturers and maintenance organizations. Limited supplier or downstream readiness may delay deployment. Technical and regulatory uncertainty can further influence purchasing decisions, particularly where specialized measurement procedures are required.

